SYSTEM pk: the release commands changelog, release and ship
ON git-at-round-8.design
REPORTS pk's message
RUNS
    changelog
    release
    ship

PLACE pk's message ONE REPORT
    SAYS What pk prints to the person: refusals, warnings, and what it did.
PLACE stdout ONE REPORT
    SAYS Where --dry-run prints the section.
PLACE .pk.json ONE OUTSIDE
    SAYS The project config; the commands read it and never write it.
PLACE the command line ONE OUTSIDE
    SAYS The flags the person gave.
PLACE CHANGELOG.md ONE LASTING IN working tree
PLACE the version files ONE LASTING IN working tree
    SAYS The JSON files changelog.versionFiles names, stamped together.
PLACE the section ONE RUN
    SAYS The changelog section generated from the commits since the last version tag.
PLACE the working branch SERIES LASTING
    SAYS The branch the run is on. In trunk flow it is the default branch.
PLACE the release branch SERIES LASTING
    SAYS release.branch, in merge flow.
PLACE origin's working branch SERIES LASTING IN origin
PLACE origin's release branch SERIES LASTING IN origin

FACT dry run
    SAYS --dry-run
FACT undo ONLY in changelog
    SAYS --undo
FACT a bump is given ONLY NOT in release
    SAYS --bump
FACT commits are excluded ONLY NOT in release
    SAYS --exclude
FACT merge flow
    SAYS release.branch is set. Empty selects trunk flow.
FACT version files are set
    SAYS changelog.versionFiles names files.
FACT the postVersion hook is set
FACT the preCommit hook is set
FACT the preRelease hook is set
FACT the prePush hook is set
FACT the preRelease hook commits ONLY the preRelease hook is set
    SAYS A preRelease hook that commits produces a commit the tag then covers.
FACT HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
    SAYS A release is pending: pk changelog committed it and pk release has not tagged it.
FACT there is a local version tag
FACT origin has a version tag ONLY NOT there is a local version tag
    SAYS A clone with no local tags, when origin has them.
FACT nothing has been released MEANS NOT there is a local version tag AND NOT origin has a version tag
    SAYS No version tag, locally or on origin.

OPEN a dry run fetches origin's tags ONLY dry run
    SAYS The changelog page says the run fetches origin's tags when it has none, and that --dry-run writes nothing. It does not say whether a dry run fetches.
OPEN pre-flight fetches the release branch ONLY merge flow
    SAYS Pre-flight fetches from origin to make its checks. The page does not say which refs.

FAULT .pk.json is invalid ABOUT .pk.json
    SAYS An unknown key or a value outside the settings fails the whole file when it loads.
FAULT the bump is not major, minor or patch ONLY a bump is given
FAULT the branch is protected
FAULT HEAD is detached
FAULT the last version tag is not in the branch's history ONLY NOT nothing has been released
    SAYS A branch rewritten after a release.
FAULT an excluded hash matches no commit ONLY commits are excluded
FAULT a version file cannot be stamped ONLY version files are set
FAULT the postVersion hook fails ONLY the postVersion hook is set
FAULT the preCommit hook fails ONLY the preCommit hook is set
FAULT the preRelease hook fails ONLY the preRelease hook is set
FAULT the prePush hook fails ONLY the prePush hook is set
FAULT the working branch is not on origin
FAULT the working branch is behind origin
FAULT the release branch cannot be resolved ONLY merge flow
FAULT the branch is not the default branch ONLY NOT merge flow
    SAYS Trunk flow refuses to run anywhere but the default branch.
FAULT switching back fails ONLY merge flow
    SAYS The switch back to the working branch fails, after the release branch and the tag are on origin.
FAULT the working branch cannot be pushed ONLY merge flow
    SAYS The push of the working branch fails, after the release branch and the tag are on origin.

SEQ changelog
    load the config
    check the bump
    check the branch
    CHOOSE
        WHEN undo
            undo the release commit
        OTHERWISE
            generate

SEQ generate
    check the tree
    fetch origin's tags
    find the last version tag
    compute the section
    CHOOSE
        WHEN dry run
            print the section
        OTHERWISE
            write and commit

SEQ write and commit
    stamp the version files
    run the postVersion hook
    write CHANGELOG.md
    run the preCommit hook
    commit the release

SEQ release
    load the config
    release the pending commit

SEQ release the pending commit
    read the Release-Tag trailer
    fetch the working branch
    fetch the release branch
    check before releasing
    run the preRelease hook
    publish WHEN NOT dry run

CHOOSE publish
    WHEN merge flow
        merge and push
    OTHERWISE
        tag and push

SEQ merge and push
    switch to the release branch
    fast-forward the release branch
    tag the release branch
    run the prePush hook
    push the release branch and the tag
    switch back to the working branch
    push the working branch

SEQ tag and push
    tag the working branch
    run the prePush hook
    push the working branch and the tag

SEQ ship
    load the config
    CHOOSE
        WHEN HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
            release the pending commit
        OTHERWISE
            SEQ
                check the bump
                check the branch
                generate
                release the pending commit WHEN NOT dry run
    SAYS Runs pk changelog then pk release as one invocation. A Release-Tag commit already pending sends ship straight to release.

ACTION load the config
    READS .pk.json
    REFUSE WHEN .pk.json is invalid
        SAYS pk commands exit 2, with a message naming the key.

ACTION check the bump WHEN a bump is given
    READS the command line
    REFUSE WHEN the bump is not major, minor or patch
        SAYS Any other --bump value is refused as a usage error, and nothing is generated.

ACTION check the branch
    READS the working branch
    REFUSE WHEN the branch is protected AND NOT dry run
    REFUSE WHEN HEAD is detached AND NOT dry run
    ACCEPT WHEN the branch is protected OR HEAD is detached
        BECAUSE A protected branch is refused, and so is a detached HEAD, except by --dry-run.

ACTION check the tree
    READS working tree
    REFUSE WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere AND NOT dry run
        SAYS A run without --dry-run refuses a dirty tree.
    ACCEPT WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere
        BECAUSE --dry-run prints the section to stdout and runs on a dirty tree.

ACTION fetch origin's tags WHEN NOT there is a local version tag AND (NOT dry run OR a dry run fetches origin's tags)
    USES fetch tags
    LATER STANDS
    BECAUSE What pk ship fetched from origin stays; the page for pk changelog says nothing else.
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer
        SAYS Only when the fetch itself fails does it stop, with the error and the hint git fetch --tags.
    ACCEPT WHEN tags is given a key twice
        BECAUSE A remote holds one tag of each name.
    TELL WHEN origin has a version tag
        SAYS Fetched tags from origin: latest is v1.2.0
    SAYS A clone with no local tags is not a first release when origin has them. pk changelog fetches origin's tags first and says so.

ACTION find the last version tag
    READS tags
    READS the working branch
    REFUSE WHEN the last version tag is not in the branch's history
        SAYS The last version tag must be in the branch's history: a branch rewritten after a release is refused, naming the tag.
    TELL WHEN nothing has been released
        SAYS No release yet: the first release covers all N commits

ACTION compute the section
    READS the working branch
    READS tags
    READS .pk.json
    CREATE the section
    TELL WHEN an excluded hash matches no commit
        SAYS A hash that matches no commit is warned about, and the run goes on.

ACTION print the section
    READS the section
    CREATE stdout FROM the section

ACTION stamp the version files WHEN version files are set
    READS the version files
    REPLACE the version files
        LATER UNDONE
    FAIL WHEN a version file cannot be stamped
        SAYS When a version file fails, nothing is committed and the tree goes back to how the run found it.

ACTION run the postVersion hook WHEN the postVersion hook is set
    READS working tree
    REPLACE working tree
        LATER UNDONE
    FAIL WHEN the postVersion hook fails
        SAYS When a hook fails, nothing is committed and the tree goes back to how the run found it, a hook's own changes included.

ACTION write CHANGELOG.md
    READS the section
    READS CHANGELOG.md
    REPLACE CHANGELOG.md
        LATER UNDONE

ACTION run the preCommit hook WHEN the preCommit hook is set
    READS working tree
    REPLACE working tree
        LATER UNDONE
    FAIL WHEN the preCommit hook fails
        SAYS When a hook fails, nothing is committed and the tree goes back to how the run found it, a hook's own changes included.

ACTION commit the release
    USES commit
        WITH the branch = the working branch
    MAKES HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
    LATER UNDONE
    SAYS Commits with a Release-Tag trailer. If the release half of pk ship fails, ship undoes the changelog commit and restores the tree.

ACTION undo the release commit
    USES reset to the commit before
        WITH the branch = the working branch
    MAKES NOT HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
    REHEARSAL dry run
    REFUSE WHEN NOT HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
    REFUSE WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere
        SAYS The tree is clean.
    REFUSE WHEN the working branch is held elsewhere
        SAYS The commit is only on the current branch: not pushed, not tagged, not merged.
    TELL WHEN dry run
        SAYS With --dry-run it makes the same checks, says what it would unwind, and changes nothing.
    SAYS --undo unwinds the release commit, restoring CHANGELOG.md and version files.

ACTION read the Release-Tag trailer
    READS the working branch
    REFUSE WHEN NOT HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
        SAYS With no Release-Tag trailer on HEAD it refuses, and says to run pk changelog first.

ACTION fetch the working branch
    USES fetch the branch
        WITH origin's branch = origin's working branch
    LATER STANDS
    BECAUSE What pk ship fetched from origin stays.
    ACCEPT WHEN remote-tracking branch holds what is kept nowhere
        BECAUSE A remote-tracking branch is a copy of origin's branch, and a fetch makes it again.
    SAYS Pre-flight fetches from origin to make these checks.

ACTION fetch the release branch WHEN merge flow AND pre-flight fetches the release branch
    USES fetch the branch
        WITH origin's branch = origin's release branch
    LATER STANDS
    BECAUSE What pk ship fetched from origin stays.
    ACCEPT WHEN remote-tracking branch holds what is kept nowhere
        BECAUSE A remote-tracking branch is a copy of origin's branch, and a fetch makes it again.

ACTION check before releasing
    READS tags
    READS working tree
    READS the working branch
    READS remote-tracking branch
    READS the release branch WHEN merge flow
    REFUSE WHEN tags already has the member
        SAYS No tag of the release's name yet.
    REFUSE WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere
        SAYS Clean tree.
    REFUSE WHEN HEAD is detached
        SAYS A branch checked out.
    REFUSE WHEN the working branch is not on origin
    REFUSE WHEN the working branch is behind origin
    REFUSE WHEN the release branch cannot be resolved
    REFUSE WHEN merge flow AND the branch cannot be fast-forwarded
        SAYS The release branch is not diverged from the working branch.
    REFUSE WHEN the branch is not the default branch
    REFUSE WHEN the last version tag is not in the branch's history
        SAYS The last version tag in the working branch's history.
    SAYS Pre-flight.

ACTION run the preRelease hook WHEN the preRelease hook is set
    READS working tree
    CREATE the working branch WHEN the preRelease hook commits
    FAIL WHEN the preRelease hook fails
    SAYS preRelease runs before the tag exists and is rehearsed by --dry-run.

ACTION switch to the release branch
    USES switch
        WITH the branch = the release branch
    LATER UNDONE
    SAYS A failure after tagging rolls back: the working branch is checked out.

ACTION fast-forward the release branch
    USES fast-forward
        WITH the branch = the release branch
        WITH the other branch = the working branch
    LATER UNDONE
    SAYS A failure after tagging rolls back: the merge is reset.

ACTION tag the release branch
    USES tag
        WITH the branch = the release branch
    MAKES there is a local version tag
    LATER UNDONE
    SAYS A failure after tagging rolls back: the local tag is deleted.

ACTION run the prePush hook WHEN the prePush hook is set
    READS tags
    FAIL WHEN the prePush hook fails
    SAYS prePush runs with the tag ref in existence, for signing or artifact builds keyed on the tag.

ACTION push the release branch and the tag
    USES push the branch and the tag
        WITH the branch = the release branch
        WITH origin's branch = origin's release branch
    LATER STANDS
    BECAUSE Once the release branch and the tag are on origin the release stands.
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer
        SAYS A failure after tagging rolls back.
    REFUSE WHEN origin rejects the push
        SAYS A failure after tagging rolls back.

ACTION switch back to the working branch
    USES switch
        WITH the branch = the working branch
    WARN WHEN switching back fails
    WARN WHEN the switch fails
    WARN WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere
    SAYS A failure to switch back is reported as a warning.

ACTION push the working branch
    USES push the branch
        WITH the branch = the working branch
        WITH origin's branch = origin's working branch
    WARN WHEN the working branch cannot be pushed
    WARN WHEN origin does not answer
    WARN WHEN origin rejects the push
    SAYS A failure to push the working branch is reported as a warning.

ACTION tag the working branch
    USES tag
        WITH the branch = the working branch
    MAKES there is a local version tag
    LATER UNDONE
    SAYS Trunk flow tags the default branch. A failure after tagging rolls back: the local tag is deleted.

ACTION push the working branch and the tag
    USES push the branch and the tag
        WITH the branch = the working branch
        WITH origin's branch = origin's working branch
    LATER STANDS
    BECAUSE Once the branch and the tag are on origin the release stands.
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer
        SAYS A failure after tagging rolls back.
    REFUSE WHEN origin rejects the push
        SAYS A failure after tagging rolls back.

EXPECT a changelog dry run writes nothing
    IN changelog
    WHEN dry run
    NEVER CHANGES
        CHANGELOG.md
        the version files
        working tree
        the working branch
    BECAUSE --dry-run prints the section without writing or committing; with --undo it changes nothing.

EXPECT a refused bump generates nothing
    WHEN the bump is not major, minor or patch
    NEVER RUNS compute the section
    NEVER CHANGES
        CHANGELOG.md
        the working branch
    BECAUSE Any other --bump value is refused as a usage error, and nothing is generated.

EXPECT a failed version file or hook leaves the tree as the run found it
    WHEN a version file cannot be stamped OR the postVersion hook fails OR the preCommit hook fails
    NEVER CHANGES
        CHANGELOG.md
        the version files
        working tree
        the working branch
    BECAUSE Nothing is committed and the tree goes back to how the run found it, a hook's own changes included.

EXPECT changelog leaves the release untagged
    IN changelog
    NEVER RUNS
        tag the release branch
        tag the working branch
    BECAUSE pk release tags it.

EXPECT a protected branch or a detached HEAD is refused
    WHEN (the branch is protected OR HEAD is detached) AND NOT dry run
    NEVER CHANGES
        CHANGELOG.md
        the working branch
        tags
        origin

EXPECT a rewritten branch is refused
    WHEN the last version tag is not in the branch's history
    NEVER CHANGES
        CHANGELOG.md
        the working branch
        the release branch
        origin

EXPECT undo refuses what it cannot unwind
    IN changelog
    WHEN undo AND (NOT HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer OR working tree holds what is kept nowhere OR the working branch is held elsewhere)
    NEVER CHANGES
        the working branch
        working tree

EXPECT release refuses with nothing pending
    IN release
    WHEN NOT HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
    NEVER CHANGES
        tags
        the working branch
        the release branch
        origin
    BECAUSE With no Release-Tag trailer on HEAD it refuses, and says to run pk changelog first.

EXPECT a release dry run merges, tags and pushes nothing
    IN release
    WHEN dry run
    NEVER CHANGES
        tags
        the release branch
        origin
    BECAUSE --dry-run validates without merging, tagging, or pushing.

EXPECT a failure after tagging rolls back
    IN release
    WHEN the prePush hook fails OR origin rejects the push
    ON FAILED
    NEVER CHANGES
        tags
        the release branch
    BECAUSE A failure after tagging rolls back: the local tag is deleted, the merge is reset, and the working branch is checked out.

EXPECT the release stands once it is on origin
    WHEN (switching back fails OR the working branch cannot be pushed) AND NOT dry run
    ON SUCCESS
    ENDS origin's release branch CREATED
    ENDS origin's tags CREATED
    BECAUSE Once the release branch and the tag are on origin the release stands: a failure to switch back or to push the working branch is reported as a warning.

EXPECT ship rolls back what it made when it fails
    IN ship
    WHEN NOT HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
    ON FAILED
    NEVER CHANGES
        CHANGELOG.md
        the version files
        the working branch
        the release branch
    BECAUSE If the release half fails, ship deletes the release tag, resets the merge, undoes the changelog commit and restores the tree.

EXPECT ship leaves a pending changelog commit alone
    IN ship
    WHEN HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
    NEVER RUNS
        commit the release
        compute the section
    BECAUSE A Release-Tag commit already pending sends ship straight to release, and is left alone.

EXPECT a ship dry run with nothing pending only previews the section
    IN ship
    WHEN dry run AND NOT HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
    ON SUCCESS
    RUNS print the section
    NEVER RUNS read the Release-Tag trailer
    BECAUSE The release half cannot be rehearsed before its changelog commit exists.

EXPECT a ship dry run with a pending commit rehearses the release
    IN ship
    WHEN dry run AND HEAD carries a valid Release-Tag trailer
    ON SUCCESS
    RUNS check before releasing
    NEVER RUNS print the section
    BECAUSE --dry-run rehearses the release when a Release-Tag commit exists.

RULE A breaking change (type!: or a BREAKING CHANGE: footer) bumps major, feat bumps minor, anything else bumps patch.
    ABOUT compute the section
RULE --bump major|minor|patch overrides the inference, and the run names the override next to the version it generates.
    ABOUT compute the section
    WHEN a bump is given
RULE --exclude drops commits by short hash before bump inference.
    ABOUT compute the section
    WHEN commits are excluded
RULE Types map to sections via changelog.types; hidden types are tracked and never listed; an empty table means the default table; showScope includes each commit's scope.
    ABOUT compute the section
RULE The first release covers the whole history from an implied v0.0.0, and its entry links to the tag's commits rather than a compare.
    ABOUT compute the section
    WHEN nothing has been released
RULE The root version field of each version file is spliced in place, formatting preserved.
    ABOUT stamp the version files
RULE The postVersion hook runs with $VERSION, with no v prefix.
    ABOUT run the postVersion hook
RULE The preCommit hook runs with $VERSION, with no v prefix.
    ABOUT run the preCommit hook
RULE The preRelease hook receives $VERSION (no v) and $TAG (with it).
    ABOUT run the preRelease hook
RULE The prePush hook receives $VERSION (no v) and $TAG (with it).
    ABOUT run the prePush hook
RULE The release commit carries a Release-Tag trailer naming the release's tag.
    ABOUT commit the release
RULE The tag's name is read from the Release-Tag trailer on HEAD.
    ABOUT read the Release-Tag trailer
RULE An invalid .pk.json makes the command exit 2 with a message naming the key.
    ABOUT load the config
RULE A --bump value other than major, minor or patch is a usage error.
    ABOUT check the bump
RULE A failed fetch of origin's tags stops with the error and the hint git fetch --tags.
    ABOUT fetch origin's tags
RULE The refusal of a rewritten branch names the tag.
    ABOUT find the last version tag
